pman @alpha 0.8

pman is a mail formatting tool. It was mainly developed for running the
ClayKit community website, but it can also be used for other purposes.
For example, it is now part of my personal website as well.

Usage: pman <mail_path> <db_path> <user> <passwd>

It only does four things:

        1. Parse the mail you submit to it
        2. Check user permissions and PAIRCODE
        3. Write to the database according to the action (if step 2 succeeded)
        4. Return the result

You should make your own copy of config.h from config.def.h.
You can manage users in config.h.

Input mail format:

        1    PAIRCODE
        2    ACTION
        3    ADDRESS
        4    TITLE
        5    CONTENT
        6    CONTENT...
        7    CONTENT......

It returns the following error codes, and 0 on success:

        #define ERR_PAIRCODE_MISMATCH  1
        #define ERR_USER_NOT_FOUND     2
        #define ERR_WRONG_PASSWORD     3
        #define ERR_NO_PERMISSION      4
        #define ERR_DB_IO              5
        #define ERR_UNKNOWN_ACTION     6

If you are interested in the ClayKit community, take a look here:
https://claykit.github.io/about

If you want to understand how it works, start by reading main().
I believe good code explains itself.
